		(uuid "0de945f0-39e0-59c3-89da-50ade6c16f15")
	)
	(text "Retain 1.5KE20A by choice, not because a 60 V low-leakage QP is absent.\nSQD50P06-15L has 50 uA max IDSS at 125 C and -60 V. The inherited\n1.5KE30A screens 43.81 V at 85 C: 1.19 V below LM2678 absolute,\n3.81 V above operating. It also requires a redesigned A5 clamp.\nSelected 1.5KE20A screens 29.20 V. R_AON is now 820R/1%; the\nBZX55C22 thermal screen requires leads <=85 C. See S3 for bounds.\nP_AON <=27.90 V is a model screen requiring bench verification.\nANY sustained P12 above 17.1 V is excluded, including alternator/\nregulator overcharge and 24 V jump start (D-OVERVOLT-04).\nThe 100/500 uA parked targets remain unchanged."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 82.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0e3c32c6-70e8-52ee-9ae4-b13c9ec4a985")
	)
	(text "GP0/GP1, GP14/GP15, GP20-GP22 and GP28 are deliberately unconnected.\nGP7 is now ISO_EN, the B2 isolation enable, confirmed free in S1.\nGP8/GP9 (UART1) and GP10 (tied DE//RE) drive onboard RS-485.\nGP13 is offered on the trimmed J3 spare/power header.\nARM, EXPIRED, PGOOD and HOLD_N stay off the GPIOs: A5-domain test\npoints only, and firmware has no ARM feedback in this revision.\nGP11 and GP12 are brought to pads per S1. ADC_VREF, 3V3_EN and VBUS\nare unconnected as fitted; VBUS has no buck connection.\nNo GPIO carries a pullup to any rail but switched 3V3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 234.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "152568d3-3533-5fa3-84e7-75975f5ed81d")
	)
	(text "The fitted cell returned the ignition LED cathode to the B16 cluster\nconductor with nothing in series, putting 4.7-5.8 mA of signal-\ndependent current through the node both ADC channels reference, which\nREV_A_INTERFACES S4 says must never become a power return. D5 and\nthat return cannot both stand. LRA-12 moves the cathode to PGND, the\narrangement DESIGN.md S3 already specified.\nWhat B16 still carries is the two divider return currents, at most\nabout 0.65 mA combined and only while the cluster is energized; those\nare intrinsic to a ratio measurement referenced to cluster ground.\nThe LED current was not.\nConsequence recorded rather than hidden: the LED now returns into the\nboard instead of off-board. It cannot reach any switched rail - the\nopto output side is in the A5 domain and galvanically separate from\nthe LED - so this removes an injection path rather than moving one.\nCTR margin at the measured 2.2k: 3.39 mA of LED current at the 9 V\ncharacterization point against 96 uA of emitter load, 15x on the\n>=50 % CTR at 5 mA. Hot CTR and the 4.5 V ON endpoint stay open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 182.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1e87e348-b36b-5db3-baa9-5c972880b4ac")
	)
