	(text "Five fitted cells, carried forward with no value changed (AS_BUILT S2).\nB2 is the only branch energized with the key out - 4.669 V open\ncircuit, 4.140 V loaded, drawing 140.8 uA of which 109.2 uA was being\nback-fed into the unpowered 3V3 rail through a forward-biased clamp.\nIt gets the series switch, upstream of the divider top as required.\nB1, C14, C11 and B11 are all ignition-fed and measured or logged dead\nwith the key out, so they meet the parked criterion with no device and\nno device leakage. Reaching the board-off-and-energized criterion\nneeds the key on AND an upstream power fault, because ignition\npresent turns QI on and powers the board; in that fault state the\nfitted 7.5k-22k series resistance bounds each branch below 0.7 mA.\nFour more relays would cost 41 mA of awake LED current and four\n10.4 x 7.5 mm packages against a fault-only benefit. Full reachable-\nstate table in LAYOUT_CLOSURE S4.\nBecause no series element enters the fuel or supply top leg, the\ncard header calibration (log.adc.fuel div=7500/4700) still has every\nterm it needs and REV_A_INTERFACES S8.2 needs no change.\nDigital divider bottoms return to PGND. Both ADC divider bottoms,\ntheir filter and clamp returns, J1.10 (B16) and Pico AGND are ONE\nnode. AGND and PGND are already joined INSIDE the Pico module, so\nthat junction is the single point: layout must NOT add a second\nboard-level bond between them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 117.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ae38147d-07f4-533e-bd1b-f86e6d9fb495")
	)
	(text "LRA-12 - what changed, and the one thing to read first"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b8fe6c50-53c2-5363-8410-2d2667f30475")
	)
	(text "Nominal 2048 s from qualified ignition loss, on its own always-on\nsupply and its own clock. The Pico cannot refresh it with HOLD,\nresets, network traffic or watchdog servicing; releasing HOLD disarms\nit, and only a qualified ignition assertion can grant it again.\nReset dominates set in the settled Boolean model. UCOUNT is reset by\nBAD OR IGN_Q and deliberately NOT by NARM, which would erase EXPIRED\nas it disarmed the latch; instead the clock stops when disarmed.\nNot covered, and stated here so nobody reads more into it: a stopped\nclock, failed timer logic, a shorted QS or QP, an ignition line stuck\nhigh, repeated raw pulses that energize QI, or external backfeed. A5\nfaults can remove power before the deadline. No SD integrity claim\nsurvives a forced cutoff.\nEvery unused CMOS input is tied to a rail (ULATCH 12 and 13 to\nground) and every package has its own 100 nF across its own supply\npins - both are layout requirements as much as BOM lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 397.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b9461a13-e3a3-5323-95b2-6da03b952fd3")
	)
	(text "X8 RESOLVED: INDEPENDENT MAXIMUM-ON CUTOFF, 2048 s  -  MAX_ON_CUTOFF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.54 677.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c070897a-5b7a-58f5-a646-9f2241fd3223")
	)
	(text "GP6 HOLD_RAW with a 47k external pulldown and the JH MAINTENANCE\nlink. Firmware latches it LOW before output enable; 4 mA drive,\n2.6 V loaded qualification target.\nQS is the series interruption the independent timer uses: drain to\nSINK, source to the QH collector, body diode blocking the sink\ndirection when off. QI remains wired straight to SINK, so raw\nignition still overrides everything. QMON senses HOLD_RAW ahead of\nJH, so opening JH releases QH without blinding the monitor.\nJH, R_EXPP/R_EXPT and the accelerated 64 s tap are three different\nthings and are labelled as such: JH is maintenance, R_EXPP is the\nproduction 2048 s selection, R_EXPT is the bench test selection and\nis DNP. Fit exactly one of R_EXPP and R_EXPT: they are two counter\noutputs and must never be shorted together."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 266.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c2e26206-a723-5fb8-8d2a-f6aefd4394d2")
	)
	(text "VEHICLE INPUTS  -  AS_BUILT S2, ratios and clamps unchanged; B2 series isolation fitted, other four branches bypassed"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 21.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb984d68-59ba-5b4c-9300-50350ca6239d")
	)
	(text "This is the LRA-06 capture with its eight electrical placeholders\nresolved. Every populated part now carries a checked footprint and\nno dashed NOT SELECTED body remains. The decisions, their\ncalculations and the residual gates are in power/LAYOUT_CLOSURE.md\nand LRA12_HANDOFF.md; read those before changing anything here.\nX1  B2 series isolation      -> ASSR-601JV + 2-FET enable\nX2-X5 other four branches    -> justified bypass, see below\nX6  qualified IGN / QREPORT  -> captured from CUTOFF_MARGIN_REVIEW S2\nX7  vehicle entry protection -> 1.5KE20A + second-stage A5 clamp\nX8  independent cutoff       -> captured from MAX_ON_CUTOFF\nJ1 board connector           -> JAE IL-AG5-14P-D3L2-A, 14-way\nQ2/R06-REV-2 opto LED return -> moved from B16 to PGND\nQ4 onboard FIGN              -> dropped; fuse belongs at the tap\nQ5 J4 service UART           -> dropped; J4 is the reset pair only\nQ6 where MAX_ON cuts HOLD    -> QS between SINK and the QH collector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc1a8dda-f930-57b7-a5ff-deb8a67a48da")
	)
	(text "Twenty-five test loops. Three separate ground loops follow the\nkeyless pattern: buck, Pico and harness end, the last on the bonded\nB16/AGND sense node. J4 shorts RUN to GND for a reset without\ncutting power.\nTP_PAON is where the <=28 V protected-rail criterion is measured.\nTP_GATE against TP_P12 is where the QP -14 to +1 V gate acceptance\nband is measured. TP_CLK32 carries the clock frequency and startup\nmeasurements the whole 2048 s arithmetic rests on.\nCurrent-sensitive nodes must be measurable without the instrument\nsupplying the current being measured, and probes must be removable\nfor the final leakage reading - a layout requirement, not only a\nprocedure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 444.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eee844e3-c9da-5ddf-b57f-e28520d11236")
	)
	(text "Voltage envelope - LRA-12R decision"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 845.82 77.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f124e809-6a2c-5a62-a616-b812f1415042")
	)
	(text "SPARE GP13 / SWITCHED POWER AND RESET"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 375.92 421.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f81653dc-1bda-51af-8e44-c001bd743d4f")
	)
